  body: "# Benefit week for Pension Credit payment\n\n**Model-assisted source interpretation; unreviewed.
    No entitlement decision or executable rule.**\n\nThe captured guidance defines a seven-day benefit
    week by its starting payment day for advance payment and its ending payment day for payment in arrears.\n\
    \n## Evidence and scope\n\n[DMG 79010–79011, PDF page 4](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/69e1035298c6c9802f7ed9e0/dmg-Chap-79.pdf#page=4)
    supports this scoped proposal. The source PDF SHA-256 is `0098a2267cb9b321cae6bf25b3493b3674c4e8cb1b859fcd6b8ae7d459323be8`.\n\
    \nThe definition alone does not decide the payment mode, start date or amount in a claimant case.\n\
    \nThe capture date, the publication page's update date and a date stated in the guidance have different
    meanings. Linked legislation and memos need their own provision, version and applicability review.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/pension-credit
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: Both definitions are explicitly scoped to SPC payment and explain the temporal unit
      used by payment guidance.
    evidence:
    - page: page/79/0004
      quote: "79010 Where SPC is paid in advance, benefit week means1 the period of seven days starting
        with the\nday on which SPC is payable to the claimant.\n\n\n                                 \
        \                                                      1 SPC Regs, reg 1(2)\n\n\nPayment in arrears\n\
        79011 Where SPC is paid in arrears, benefit week means1 the period of seven days ending with the
        day\non which SPC is payable to the claimant.\n\n\n                                          \
        \                                             1 SPC Regs, reg 1(2)"
      locator: DMG 79010–79011
